      \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n      \"witness_indices\": [\n        24\n      ],\n      \"valid_witness_indices\": [\n        24\n      ],\n      \"witness_complete\": true,\n      \"comparison_complete\": true,\n      \"missing_indices\": [],\n      \"evaluated_indices\": [\n        7,\n        14,\n        24,\n        26\n      ],\n      \"outside_applicability_indices\": [],\n      \"correlations\": {\n        \"7\": {\n          \"status\": \"matched\",\n          \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n          \"matched_indices\": [\n            1\n          ],\n          \"alias_indices\": {\n            \"admitted\": 1\n          }\n        },\n        \"14\": {\n          \"status\": \"matched\",\n          \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n          \"matched_indices\": [\n            8\n          ],\n          \"alias_indices\": {\n            \"admitted\": 8\n          }\n        },\n        \"24\": {\n          \"status\": \"matched\",\n          \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n          \"matched_indices\": [\n            17\n          ],\n          \"alias_indices\": {\n            \"admitted\": 17\n          }\n        },\n        \"26\": {\n          \"status\": \"matched\",\n          \"reason\": \"Declared prerequisites established\",\n          \"matched_indices\": [\n            18\n          ],\n          \"alias_indices\": {\n            \"admitted\": 18\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"diagnostics\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"Independent applicability, correlated prerequisites and fully observed result comparison\",\n      \"confirmed\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"adaptations\": [\n    \"Use captured in-memory TestLogDB instead of engine LogDB and deterministic delivery queues instead of transport. No crashes or storage failures occur.\",\n    \"Driver persists State and EntriesToSave before any message delivery, applies bootstrap config/no-op entries, acknowledges Update and reports applied index.\",\n    \"Private state is read only for prefix/admission diagnostics; all protocol state changes use Peer methods.\"\n  ],\n  \"conditions\": {\n    \"plan_uncertainties\": [\n      \"This observes the actual Peer readiness output, not client RequestState completion or application read data.\",\n      \"The serial control and overlap histories establish no crash recovery or membership-transition result.\",\n      \"No success deadline is asserted; a missing result remains incomplete rather than proving infinite stalling.\"\n    ],\n    \"grounding_unresolved\": [],\n    \"review_limitations\": []\n  },\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed\"\n  ],\n  \"boundaries\": [\n    \"A guarantee that every read succeeds rather than times out.\",\n    \"Client ReadLocal endpoint, stale data, linearizability violation, or global progress consequence.\",\n    \"Crash recovery and real storage/network behavior.\",\n    \"This observes the actual Peer readiness output, not client RequestState completion or application read data.\",\n    \"The serial control and overlap histories establish no crash recovery or membership-transition result.\",\n    \"No success deadline is asserted; a missing result remains incomplete rather than proving infinite stalling.\"\n  ],\n  \"review_ids\": [],\n  \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n  \"correspondence\": null,\n  \"reviewed_complete\": false,\n  \"bounded_complete\": true,\n  \"confirmed\": false,\n  \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_test\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-read-context\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"framework_revision\": \"audit-products-v45\",\n  \"finding_ids\": {\n    \"read-context\": \"47714505919d42d0b5ccb06af227cc97\"\n  },\n  \"finding_id\": \"47714505919d42d0b5ccb06af227cc97\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nss=['s-context-contract','s-update-contract','s-launch-validation','s-bootstrap-prefix','s-peer','s-test-storage','s-test-storage-append','s-send-origin','s-read-queue','s-read-replies','s-read-forward','s-heartbeat-producer','s-read-consumer']\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='Reviewed fixed artifact 6c55c140b1a0408fa1d92056824e1c89 (version 2), its plan, harness, claim-read-context version 1 and raw execution eae47b2a7b964503b32c9881fc487819. The increment only assigns distinct bootstrap addresses required by checkLaunchRequest; the earlier failed run remains initialization failure, not protocol evidence. Launch creates the bootstrap configurations, harvested committed configurations are applied via Peer, and only node 1 is ticked until an actual vote exchange elects it. Generated no-op replication reaches commit/applied index 4 at term 2 at every peer. State and entries are copied to TestLogDB before outgoing messages are delivered; Commit acknowledges the exported update, then NotifyRaftLastApplied reports actual simulated application of bootstrap/no-op entries. There are no application commands or crash faults; this substitution is adequate for the scoped Peer identity proposition, not durability. The read history contains one ReadIndex at each origin, forwarded by actual send, then actual leader heartbeat and follower response producers; no confirming support is synthesized. The accepted controlled schedule delays first-context heartbeat delivery while second-context traffic drains and then delivers all held first-context traffic. Peer contract does not impose a receive FIFO prerequisite; the check is at that boundary and does not demonstrate this exact ordering through the concrete transport. Each read_admitted event follows real leader pending admission, and each read_result copies an exported ReadyToRead before Commit clears it. Scenario plus origin uniquely associates each result to its single invocation, independently of SystemCtx, so the wrong context is retained rather than filtered out. High and Low are compared as a lossless decimal pair. Four comparisons were reached without parse errors: serial origin 2 returned 901:201 and serial origin 3 returned 902:302; overlap origin 2 admitted 901:201 but returned 902:302 at index/applied 4, while overlap origin 3 correctly returned 902:302. The valid witness is event 24 correlated with admission 17. Both histories emitted one result per origin and ended with leader pending count zero, after all held messages drained. The index rewrite is allowed and is not the oracle. The interface duty that SystemCtx identifies the previous ReadIndex batch grounds identity preservation, independently of successful-read timing. Source readIndex.confirm releases the prefix, and the remote branch takes m.Hint instead of s.ctx, explaining the same-history observation. No correspondence issue was found for this narrow measured proposition.',counterevidence=['Serial forwarding preserves both contexts; the failure requires overlapping queued reads and later-context confirmation in this witness.','The local completion branch uses each status context; this is not a finding about all ReadIndex completions.','Earlier delayed heartbeat responses were eventually delivered and did not produce another readiness record in the drained trace. This is finite observation, not proof of infinite stalling.'],limitations=['Observed endpoint is Peer.GetUpdate ReadyToReads, not node pendingReadIndex notification, client timeout, or ReadLocal application data.','In-memory persistence and controlled message queues substitute storage and concrete transport; no real-network reachability or crash result is established.','No changing membership, leadership transition, context collision, or multiple reads at the same origin is exercised.','No numeric progress deadline or stale-read/linearizability violation follows from the identity mismatch.'],report_title='重叠转发读取的响应标识被替换',report_answer='在固定任期和三投票成员下，后一个读取的心跳确认释放两个请求时，节点 2 请求的 901:201 被返回为节点 3 的 902:302。串行对照正常；已观察到 Peer 层标识不匹配，未证明应用读取过期或客户端无限等待。')\np=dict(action='review',artifact_id='6c55c140b1a0408fa1d92056824e1c89',rationale='Review the successful repaired execution and its complete identity mismatch witness; preserve the failed predecessor and endpoint limitations.',review_items=[item],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['c5a8b964cd314bab88b6ac6c16df1333','b-read-deliver','f-read-support','eae47b2a7b964503b32c9881fc487819','s-read-replies','s-context-contract'],answered='The fixed three-voter stable-term Peer history validates the remote response identity discrepancy: confirming the later queued context causes the earlier origin to receive the later context in ReadyToRead. The serial control preserves identity. All four operations have separately correlated admission and result events; the earlier overlap origin is the sole mismatching witness.',remaining=['Independent question: whether a concrete transport schedule and node/client consumers exhibit request timeout or another endpoint consequence.','Independent frontier: outstanding read support eligibility across membership transitions without term reset.'],understanding='updated',rationale='This answers the scoped released-read identity question by actual producer execution and recipient output. The cause is consistent with the remote context selection source. Broader safety and progress claims remain excluded, and further variants are not necessary to establish this observed discrepancy.'))\njson.dump(p,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_20-05-00-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
